#
# CQ1 + CQ9 (INHABITED-COMPETENCY.md, INHABITED-IDENTITY.md): for one
# gmeow:SubjectLineage, an affirming ('same', the atman reading) and a denying
# ('different', the anatta reading) gmeow:IdentityContinuityAssessment COEXIST as
# asserted verdicts — the denial (CQ9) is a positive verdict, never the mere
# absence of an affirmation, and the affirmation (CQ1) does not collapse the two
# distinct gmeow:SubjectStage nodes to owl:sameAs (Principle 9). Asserted lane:
# a gmeow:ContinuityDetermination (a SubKind of IdentityContinuityAssessment)
# is NOT matched without reasoning, so the decisional layer stays out and only
# the two descriptive assessments surface.
PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
SELECT ?verdict WHERE {
    ?a a gmeow:IdentityContinuityAssessment ;
       gmeow:observedFeature <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/examples/inhabitation/lillithLineage> ;
       gmeow:continuityVerdict ?verdict .
}
ORDER BY ?verdict
